## Apolar setup

Let

```text
R=k[x,y,z]
```

and let `I` be the component-20 Artinian ideal from UST.G3FO. Use the divided-
power dual of `R`, so multiplication in `R` is dual to coefficient-free
contraction in the inverse system `I^perp`.

The dual dimensions are

```text
degree:       15  16  17  18  19  20
dim I^perp:   36  11   6   3   1   0.
```

## Mixed-degree primitive source

The inverse system has exactly 20 minimal primitives:

```text
18 primitives in degree 15,
 1 primitive  in degree 16,
 1 primitive  in degree 19.
```

The degree-19 primitive has derivative-tower dimensions

```text
1, 3, 6, 10, 15
```

in degrees `19,18,17,16,15`. The first derivatives of the degree-16
primitive span three further directions in degree 15. Therefore

```text
I^perp_15
  = 18 degree-15 primitives
    + 3 first derivatives of the degree-16 primitive
    + 15 fourth derivatives of the degree-19 primitive,

dim I^perp_15 = 18+3+15 = 36.
```

All three summands are independent at every fiber. Their apolar annihilator in
`R_15` is exactly the archived 100-dimensional component-20 kernel:

```text
136 = 100 + 36.
```

## Why this matters

The finite rank-36 quotient is no longer an unexplained complement of a
100-plane. It is the derivative closure of one mixed-degree inverse-system
module of type 20. This also explains why the earlier single-catalecticant
probe failed: one scalar inverse polynomial has the wrong source type. The
correct finite apolar object needs the displayed `18+1+1` primitive grading.

The coincidence between socle type 20 and the component label is a useful
structural clue, but no physical or representation-theoretic identification
is claimed from the number alone.

## Promotion audit

The primitive source uses 2,811 field coefficients, or 16,866 sextic
power-basis slots per prime. Seven-prime construction and an eighth-prime
holdout yield:

```text
16,866 coefficients checked,
3,960 holdout passes,
3,940 passing zeros,
20 passing units,
0 passing nontrivial coefficients.
```

Thus the mixed-degree source must still be derived geometrically; blind
small-height coefficient reconstruction does not promote it.

## New frontier

The most economical characteristic-zero target is now the primitive source,
not the 100 kernel vectors or the 49/20 differential columns. Derive over
`Q(gamma)`:

1. the single degree-19 primitive;
2. the single degree-16 primitive modulo its ten inherited directions;
3. the 18-dimensional degree-15 primitive lane;
4. their divided-power derivative closure;
5. the equality of its degree-15 annihilator with the exact G3EX source map.

The selected G3FK four-normal Cayley/Koszul source must supply those objects
with the correct Cox shifts. Once this is done, the `100/36` component theorem
is characteristic-zero rather than finite-fiber evidence.

This does not yet prove global H02 rank equality, the continuum/cohesive/HYM
intertwiner or a selected physical endpoint.

